From 9ecaa869c1e9640ae78572e505fc0e771e01c39d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim Carney <tim.carney@cargt.com>
Date: Thu, 28 May 2026 12:05:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] cargt/imx93_00363: add shared LPDDR4X timing infrastructure

Extract arrays shared across all timing variants into a common translation
unit: ddrphy_pie for each speed, fsp1/fsp2 message blocks, and
ddrphy_trained_csr count macros.

Add per-variant inc files under include/ containing only the arrays that
differ between variants (ddrc_cfg, fsp0_cfg, ddrphy_cfg, etc.) so timing
.c files reduce to thin wrappers referencing only variant-specific data.

Add optimized_timings_for_reference/ as review copies of the fully
assembled timing sources (not compiled into SPL).

Update Makefile to compile cargt_lpddr4x_timing_shared.o.
